   "source": [
    "**Duplicate Values:**\n",
    "\n",
    "Looking at the cells above, we can see that there are no exact duplicate rows in either the playbyplay or player_stats dataframes. However, this does not rule out the possibility of having the same play or player id listed that differ in some other column. Therefore, a check was ran using natural keys of (play_id + game_id) for playbyplay and (player_id + game_id) for player_stats to make sure that there were no duplicate keys that were used with differing columns. For playbyplay, those keys were chosen as a combination because the play_id may reset and be reused each game but then the game_ids would be different. In each check the repeating natural keys chosen came up as 0, so we have determined there are no duplicate values to worry about. Therefore, we did not need to change the dataframes."
   ]
