   "source": [
    "# run and pass plays average success rate\n",
    "sns.barplot(data = snsq1, x = \"success\", y = \"play_type\")\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "67520cf3",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Success rate is defined as how often each play keeps the offense on track, defined as gaining at least 40% of needed yards on 1st, 60% on 2nd, and 100% on 3rd. Pass plays had a higher average success rate than running plays in 2025 based on this chart."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "758c5929",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Question 2: Do the stats suggest punting or going for it on 4th down?\n",
    "\n",
    "I think the best way to approach this with the current data sets would be to look at average EPA gained when grouping run/pass plays together versus punting, grouped by the distance left (since it obviously matters how many yards are needed). For this, I want to look at the EPA/Play distribution specifically for 4th downs for each type without regards to yardage just yet."
   ]
  },
