    "# plot 4th down epa/play grouped by play type\n",
    "fig = px.box(fourthOnlyPbp, x = \"epa\", y = \"play_type\")\n",
    "fig.update_layout(width = 800, height = 600)\n",
    "fig"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "ad1fb91d",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "The distributions grouped by play type are really varied. Punting is generally a negative play with a median around -0.1 EPA, but with the nature of punting it's usually a minor negative or positive, with a few outliers for what I imagine are bad punts (negative side) or great punts and muffs (positive side). The median for run EPA is very high at +1.9, likely because of 4th and short conversions where teams often run on, but sharply drops in the first quantile down to -2.5. Passing is the most unusual one to me, where the median is -1.0, but the upper quartile is larger than the run stats. I'm guessing this is caused by 4th and longs where there's little chance to convert anyway."
   ]
  },
